friends of a man killed in a random  shooting are sharing members memories of  that 35 year old they say curtis abraham  was the victim of an attack at a gas  station and police eventually tracked  down the suspect 12 hours later not far  from where the shooting happened and  sasha loftis is at that gas station  tonight with how curtis is being  remembered sasha  denise and brian candles are lit here  outside the convenience store where  friends say curtis abraham lost his life  in that senseless shooting now they're  doing their best to remember the amazing  person they say he was  he brought a certain  aspect to everybody's life of happiness  a longtime friend of curtis abraham  describes what he brought to everyone in  his life he moved out here to get to do  better and he excelled at that dozens  gathered to honor the 35 year old  thursday after quentin adams tells 8  news now curtis was shot and killed when  someone randomly opened fire at this  convenience store in the southwest  valley  the suspect was later arrested after an  hours long search and a barricade  situation we are very thankful for the  public's assistance it is because of the  public's assistance and  outpouring that we were able to put this  case  or solve this case and arrest the  suspect officers say they're glad to  have what they believe is a violent  criminal off the streets but those who  loved curtis say it doesn't change how  quickly he was taken from them you never  know when somebody's going to be gone  tomorrow don't take a text message don't  take a phone call don't take anything  for granted but they know the light he  shined on their world will never be  forgotten it shows you how far one  person can reach and what type of impact  that one person can make on the world  police have not shared the identity of  the suspect in this case but they did  say that a tip led to his arrest they  also added that the suspect's family  cooperated with the investigation  reporting live tonight 